Let prime generation yield, so that RSA key generation does not stop the
browser.

Why: script's crypto.subtle.generateKey for RSA (src/net/webcrypto.c,
src/js/natives_crypto.c) generates two primes of 512 to 2048 bits,
which takes seconds on a 1 GHz G4. Aura runs the generation on a
coroutine (or a worker's own stack) and leaves it between steps; the
library has no point at which it hands control back, so this patch adds
one.

What: with the option AURA_MBEDTLS_YIELD (set in
third_party/mbedtls-config/aura_crypto_config.h), mbedtls_mpi_gen_prime
calls aura_mbedtls_yield() before each candidate and mpi_miller_rabin
before each round. The embedder defines the function
(src/net/tls_platform.c). A nonzero return abandons the generation with
MBEDTLS_ERR_MPI_ALLOC_FAILED, which the PSA layer reports as
PSA_ERROR_INSUFFICIENT_MEMORY; the key slot is released as for any
failed generation. Without the option the library is unchanged.

To drop it: delete this file, remove AURA_MBEDTLS_YIELD from
third_party/mbedtls-config, remove au_tls_set_yield and
aura_mbedtls_yield from src/net/tls_platform.c and their callers in
src/js/natives_crypto.c, and run apply.sh.

diff -ruN a/tf-psa-crypto/drivers/builtin/src/bignum.c b/tf-psa-crypto/drivers/builtin/src/bignum.c
--- a/tf-psa-crypto/drivers/builtin/src/bignum.c
+++ b/tf-psa-crypto/drivers/builtin/src/bignum.c
@@ -2059,6 +2059,23 @@

 #if defined(MBEDTLS_GENPRIME)

+#if defined(AURA_MBEDTLS_YIELD)
+/* Aura patch: a cooperative yield point, defined by the embedder
+ * (src/net/tls_platform.c). Prime generation calls it before each
+ * candidate and each Miller-Rabin round, so a long key generation can
+ * let other work run. A nonzero return abandons the generation. */
+int aura_mbedtls_yield(void);
+#define AURA_YIELD_POINT()                          \
+    do {                                            \
+        if (aura_mbedtls_yield() != 0) {            \
+            ret = MBEDTLS_ERR_MPI_ALLOC_FAILED;     \
+            goto cleanup;                           \
+        }                                           \
+    } while (0)
+#else
+#define AURA_YIELD_POINT() do { } while (0)
+#endif
+
 /* Largest "small prime" tested. If this is ever changed, must update:
  * - the product below obviously,
  * - the documentation and tests of mbedtls_mpi_is_prime_ext() about this limit,
@@ -2167,6 +2184,7 @@
     MBEDTLS_MPI_CHK(mbedtls_mpi_shift_r(&R, s));

     for (i = 0; i < rounds; i++) {
+        AURA_YIELD_POINT();
         /*
          * pick a random A, 1 < A < |X| - 1
          */
@@ -2302,6 +2320,7 @@
     }

     while (1) {
+        AURA_YIELD_POINT();
         MBEDTLS_MPI_CHK(mbedtls_mpi_fill_random(X, n * ciL, f_rng, p_rng));
         /* make sure generated number is at least (nbits-1)+0.5 bits (FIPS 186-4 §B.3.3 steps 4.4, 5.5) */
         if (X->p[n-1] < CEIL_MAXUINT_DIV_SQRT2) {
